; Nitram Micro Mono: 5x5 glyph RAM initialization for vga_driver.vhd
; Source: https://github.com/nitram509/nitram-micro-font
; Font data: sources/nitram_micro_mono.json (original 256 CP437-style indices)
; Source SHA256: 3b24131ff3b1c11c7ceee23cb7af2242b0e91e417410f95d5b33813f36625206
; Memory size: 512 words x 16 bits. Two consecutive words per glyph.
; Glyph n: local RAM words 2*n and 2*n+1; CPU addresses xE000+2*n and xE001+2*n.
; Word 0 rows 0/1/2: bits 14:10 / 9:5 / 4:0. Bit 15 is zero.
; Word 1 rows 3/4: bits 9:5 / 4:0. Bits 15:10 are zero.
; Highest bit in each 5-bit row is the LEFTMOST pixel.
; Original character order preserved: space=x20, 0=x30, A=x41, a=x61.
; Keyboard FIFO codes require translation to these font indices.
; Example screen word x0741 displays a white A on a black background.
;
